  "schema_version": 1,
  "source_reasoning": [
    "NN RpcCall entry IOException becomes RemoteException(IOException). The existing JUnit aborts at setup/rename and no postfault NN target appears.",
    "The target is reached inside FSDirRenameOp.RenameOperation after RPC ingress. Edit-log rename/sync is after the in-memory target.",
    "The non-HA ClientProtocol proxy has a retry wrapper, but its default retry policy is disabled. RetryUtils retries a local IOException when explicitly enabled, while RemoteException apart from SafeModeException is not retried.",
    "ClientNamenodeProtocolTranslatorPB.rename converts the local ServiceException cause back to IOException via ShadedProtobufHelper.ipc. The 20,1 retry spec permits one retry.",
    "A method-aware beforeDoor at Client.Connection.sendRpcRequest before rpcSend selects ClientProtocol.rename and throws before queueing. A single retry could then send the rename and reach NN replaceChild after the fault. This remains unverified."
  ],
